Description: fix explicit NVMe namespace firmware boot paths
 Namespace realization moves devices from the PCI controller to the subsystem
 bus. Bind bootindex to the original controller and the assigned NSID after
 realization, including shared namespaces, and remove or reroute those entries
 when their namespace or controller disappears. Keep QOM updates bound to the
 same path. Exercise reset, removal, automatic IDs, private/shared namespaces
 and multiple paths in the firmware boot-order qtest. Encode NSIDs in hex,
 as required for matching UEFI device paths. Clear the subsystem namespace
 slot on removal so reusing an NSID does not retain a freed namespace.
Forwarded: no

